# Git — no direct commits

**Do not commit in this repository.** Only give the user a commit message they can apply themselves.

## Forbidden

```text
git commit, git add (for committing), git push, git commit --amend
git rebase, git reset --hard, git checkout --, SKIP HOOKS (--no-verify)
```

Read-only git is allowed: `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`.

## When work is ready

1. Confirm docs + tests are part of the change (do not propose a commit without them).
2. Draft **one** message (1–2 sentences, **why** not file lists). Match existing history: descriptive prose, not ticket IDs unless the user used them.
3. Show it in a fenced block. Do not run `git commit`.

```text
Add public registration so traders can create accounts without an admin.

Document the register story and cover the handler with unit tests.
```

If the user says “commit this”, still **do not commit** — return the message again.

If they insist on an exception, stop and confirm they want **you** to run `git commit`. Default remains: message only.
